{"text": "HERMES Mail/X is an email client built for power users, written in 100% Cocoa and inspired by HERMES Mail and Eudora for Windows.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "Nicholas Edward Werner-Matavka is the creator of HERMES Mail/X.", "dimensions": ["team"], "type": "team_member", "primary_dimension": "team", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "The project HERMES Mail/X was funded by 28 backers who pledged CA$ 1,669.", "dimensions": ["strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "funding_source", "primary_dimension": "strategy", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "The funding goal for HERMES Mail/X was CA$ 1,250.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "The funding period for HERMES Mail/X was from December 19, 2018, to February 17, 2019.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "Eudora was originally written by Steve Dorner for the Macintosh in 1988.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "Eudora was named in honor of American author Eudora Welty.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "Eudora was bought out by Qualcomm in 1991.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "Eudora was re-written for PCs after its initial release on Macintosh.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "Qualcomm discontinued Eudora in 2006 amidst shifting corporate priorities.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "Eudora OSE was introduced as a replacement for the original Eudora but was not well received.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "Eudora still has a fan base, which is why HERMES Mail/X is being developed.", "dimensions": ["objectives"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 0, "char_start": 0, "char_end": 1800}}
{"text": "Qualcomm Eudora was killed off in 2006 amidst shifting corporate priorities.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 1, "char_start": 1400, "char_end": 3200}}
{"text": "Eudora OSE replaced Qualcomm Eudora but was not well received and soon died as well.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 1, "char_start": 1400, "char_end": 3200}}
{"text": "The code for Eudora was open-sourced and given to the Computer History Museum this year.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 1, "char_start": 1400, "char_end": 3200}}
{"text": "Development of Eudora was picked up by a team of C++ programmers led by Nicholas Edward Werner-Matavka.", "dimensions": ["team"], "type": "team_member", "primary_dimension": "team", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 1, "char_start": 1400, "char_end": 3200}}
{"text": "The program was re-christened Hermes due to legal encumbrances preventing the use of the Eudora name.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 1, "char_start": 1400, "char_end": 3200}}
{"text": "Hermes is named after the Greek personification of business and patron deity of messengers.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 1, "char_start": 1400, "char_end": 3200}}
{"text": "The Windows version of Hermes is planned to be released in Q1 2019.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "feasibility"], "type": "milestone", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 1, "char_start": 1400, "char_end": 3200}}
{"text": "During a previous Kickstarter campaign, there were requests to resurrect Eudora for Apple Mac.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 1, "char_start": 1400, "char_end": 3200}}
{"text": "The original plan was to rewrite the user interface of the Windows version to make it compatible with multiple platforms.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 1, "char_start": 1400, "char_end": 3200}}
{"text": "The team is debating two alternatives for the user interface design of Hermes.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 1, "char_start": 1400, "char_end": 3200}}
{"text": "Eudora was actually two programs, written in different languages (C and C++) on separate platforms (x86 and Power PC).", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 2, "char_start": 2800, "char_end": 4600}}
{"text": "One idea is to abandon Macintosh Eudora and to write a Macintosh interface from scratch, using the Windows version's code.", "dimensions": ["strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "tech_route", "primary_dimension": "strategy", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 2, "char_start": 2800, "char_end": 4600}}
{"text": "The benefit of using the Windows version's code for the Macintosh interface is that it is economical in respect to time and cost.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 2, "char_start": 2800, "char_end": 4600}}
{"text": "The drawback of using the Windows version's code is that Macintosh Eudora users might be unused to the Windows version.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 2, "char_start": 2800, "char_end": 4600}}
{"text": "The alternative idea is to open a separate project with the code coming from the Macintosh version.", "dimensions": ["strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "tech_route", "primary_dimension": "strategy", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 2, "char_start": 2800, "char_end": 4600}}
{"text": "The benefit of using the Macintosh version's code is that it is more specific to OS X and UNIX.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 2, "char_start": 2800, "char_end": 4600}}
{"text": "The Macintosh code is less complete, obsolescent, and uses obsolete tools like the CodeWarrior integrated development environment.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 2, "char_start": 2800, "char_end": 4600}}
{"text": "The project is currently pursuing both ideas for the Macintosh interface.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy"], "type": "pipeline", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 2, "char_start": 2800, "char_end": 4600}}
{"text": "It may be that the team won't know until shortly before launch which version will receive official support.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "feasibility"], "type": "milestone", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 2, "char_start": 2800, "char_end": 4600}}
{"text": "The development of the eMail client formerly known as QUALCOMM Eudora is ongoing.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "The team is currently pursuing two approaches for the development of the eMail client.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "The team may not know which version of the eMail client will receive official support until shortly before launch.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "The team anticipates that they will likely determine early on if one of the alternatives is impossible.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "The new Eudora's display of rich-text messages must change.", "dimensions": ["objectives"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "Eudora's interface relies on an outdated and prohibitively expensive toolkit.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "The team needs to support Eudora 7 until the release of its successor.", "dimensions": ["objectives"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "Writing the new Eudora for Macintosh is expected to be challenging.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "The team made commitments to their Windows backers and users regarding the development of the eMail client.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "The team promises Macintosh backers and users that HERMES Mail/X will support Unicode (UTF-8).", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "HERMES Mail/X will have the ability to send messages in every left-to-right alphabetic language.", "dimensions": ["objectives"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 3, "char_start": 4200, "char_end": 6000}}
{"text": "HERMES Mail/X is a continuation of Eudora in Cocoa for the Mac by Nicholas Edward Werner-Matavka.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 4, "char_start": 5600, "char_end": 7400}}
{"text": "HERMES Mail/X will support Unicode (UTF-8) and the ability to send messages in every left-to-right alphabetic language.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 4, "char_start": 5600, "char_end": 7400}}
{"text": "HERMES Mail/X will include a spelling checker or support the spelling checker included in OS X.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 4, "char_start": 5600, "char_end": 7400}}
{"text": "HERMES Mail/X will be a successor to Eudora that will run on all computers with OS X (32-bit and 64-bit).", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 4, "char_start": 5600, "char_end": 7400}}
{"text": "There will be a stopgap measure between the release of HERMES Mail and Mail/X, allowing users to run the successor to Eudora on their Mac.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 4, "char_start": 5600, "char_end": 7400}}
{"text": "HERMES Mail for Windows now sends and receives messages, although it is unsuitable for general release.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 4, "char_start": 5600, "char_end": 7400}}
{"text": "Another variant of HERMES Mail does not have message-sending capability, but the interface has been built from the ground up.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 4, "char_start": 5600, "char_end": 7400}}
{"text": "The HERMES SSL Extensions are in wide use and work correctly when installed properly.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 4, "char_start": 5600, "char_end": 7400}}
{"text": "The team acknowledges that some details published about HERMES Mail were wrong or impossible.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 4, "char_start": 5600, "char_end": 7400}}
{"text": "The team aims to correct the oversight regarding HERMES Mail/X due to the number of requests for platform support.", "dimensions": ["objectives"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 4, "char_start": 5600, "char_end": 7400}}
{"text": "HERMES Mail/X aims to support Mac OS X and UNIX workstations.", "dimensions": ["objectives"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 5, "char_start": 7000, "char_end": 8800}}
{"text": "Users will need to install HERMES Mail/Win and the Wine compatibility layer for Mac OS X support.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 5, "char_start": 7000, "char_end": 8800}}
{"text": "The previous campaign raised sufficient money to create a quality product.", "dimensions": ["strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "funding_source", "primary_dimension": "strategy", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 5, "char_start": 7000, "char_end": 8800}}
{"text": "Creating a new product presents challenges due to transitions in the Apple architecture since 2005.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "risk", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 5, "char_start": 7000, "char_end": 8800}}
{"text": "The Mac has a lower market share than the PC.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 5, "char_start": 7000, "char_end": 8800}}
{"text": "The biggest hurdle for the project is manpower.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "risk", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "In the 1990s, the Macintosh was not technically stable.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "risk", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "Major users of the Macintosh in the 1990s were in education.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "Programmers for the Macintosh were harder to find in the 1990s.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "risk", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "The Macintosh has become entirely divorced from its heritage and is now UNIX with graphics tweaks.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "Programmers for UNIX are easier to find but more expensive to employ.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "risk", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "Eudora was originally written for 1990's Macs and has undergone multiple porting processes.", "dimensions": ["innovation"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "innovation", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "The original code of Eudora was written for CodeWarrior, which is no longer supported.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "risk", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "Carbon is outdated and must be transitioned to Cocoa.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "risk", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "The project will need to employ more programmers this time around.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "resource", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "The programmers will come at a more expensive price.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "The project aims to create a product that will improve the experience for Apple users.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 6, "char_start": 8400, "char_end": 10200}}
{"text": "The project is called HERMES Mail/X, which is a continuation of Eudora in Cocoa for the Mac.", "dimensions": ["objectives"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 7, "char_start": 9800, "char_end": 11600}}
{"text": "The project is led by Nicholas Edward Werner-Matavka.", "dimensions": ["team"], "type": "team_member", "primary_dimension": "team", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 7, "char_start": 9800, "char_end": 11600}}
{"text": "The project is currently 107% funded with 10 days left.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"suspect_numeric": false, "proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 7, "char_start": 9800, "char_end": 11600}}
{"text": "The project aims to alleviate issues faced by Apple Mail users.", "dimensions": ["objectives", "strategy", "feasibility"], "type": "market", "primary_dimension": "objectives", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 7, "char_start": 9800, "char_end": 11600}}
{"text": "The project is hosted on Kickstarter.", "dimensions": ["feasibility"], "type": "other", "primary_dimension": "feasibility", "meta": {"proposal_id": "kt8__openai", "chunk_index": 7, "char_start": 9800, "char_end": 11600}}
